+
+#### Pruning merged branches and worktrees
+
+Finished branches and worktrees are removed for you, so they do not pile up after every merged pull request. This runs in three places, with no flag to remember:
+
+- `ta cleanup` (the `branches` group)
+- right after `ta draft watch` or `ta draft merge` sees your pull request merged
+- the daemon's periodic cleanup, even when `[cleanup] auto = "off"`
+
+```bash
+ta cleanup --only branches --dry-run   # List each local branch, the verdict and the reason. Changes nothing.
+ta cleanup --only branches             # Delete the safe ones, ask about the rest
+```
+
+The pull request state comes from your VCS host (for GitHub, `gh pr list`), not from `git branch -d` or `git cherry`. Those two call every squash-merged branch unmerged, because a squash merge rewrites the commits.
+
+A local branch is deleted without asking when its pull request is merged and the branch has no commits beyond the pull request's head, or when its tip is already inside the default branch. A worktree that has the branch checked out is removed first, but only if it is clean.
+
+These are never deleted, and are put to you as a question instead:
+
+- a branch with an open pull request, no pull request, or commits beyond the merged pull request's head
+- a branch whose worktree has uncommitted or untracked files (the question lists the files)
+- a branch that points at the same commit as the default branch with no merged pull request to explain it, since it may be new work
+
+The current branch and the default branch are never touched. If `gh` is missing or not logged in, the pull request state is "unknown" and only branches already inside the default branch are deleted.
+
+Each deletion is recorded with the branch name and its tip commit in `.ta/cleanup/branches.jsonl` and in `.ta/audit.jsonl`, so it is recoverable:
+
+```bash
+git branch feature/my-change 3f2c9a1d...   # the "recover" line from the log
+```
+
+Remote branches are never deleted (GitHub removes them when the pull request merges). Remote branches whose pull request was closed without merging are listed in the cleanup report so you can decide. To turn branch pruning off, set `branches = false` under `[cleanup]` in `.ta/workflow.toml`.
+
